The theory-to-structure relation is:
$
  "Current + Standing" -> "one machine-owned transition",
$
$
  "machine-owned transition" -> "successor + immediate radiation".
$
The host or CUDA executor supplies physical conduct *inside* that transition. It does not receive
a receipt and reconstruct the successor. A world may mutate material and later present the
consequence as new Current. Journals, hashes, observers, forests, and reports testify after the
commit; they are not causal owners.

== Production boundary <j2-production>

The production path is

```text
life::direct::current_world
  -> soma_membrane::LiveCurrentMachine::receive_with
  -> host or CUDA executor inside the atomic call
  -> machine-validated successor
  -> ContemporaryRadiation
  -> possible later world consequence
```

The machine owns validation, same-prestate enactment, successor preparation, commitment of
Standing and lineages, departure, and radiation. The executor may discover that a physical
aperture is insufficient and request a larger one. A retry is lawful only while the predecessor is
unchanged and nothing has committed.

#proposition[
  Suppose an event attempt is a pure physical evaluation of fixed $(S_t,K_e)$ until the machine
  validates and commits. If every failed aperture attempt leaves $S_t$ unchanged, then any number
  of resource retries followed by one successful commit is observationally equivalent at the
  machine boundary to one sufficiently provisioned attempt.
]

#proof[
  Every attempt evaluates the same arguments. Failed attempts have no visibility edge and make no
  state change. The first validated attempt determines the only committed successor and radiation,
  so the retry history is absent from the causal machine state except as optional testimony.
]

This is not a general claim about arbitrary side-effecting retries. It is a consequence of the
specific uncommitted-event boundary.

== World consequence and joint rest <j2-world>

In the native world-rest cell, a declared forward hand changed a named register. The mutation
returned as genuinely later native Current. Before that current crossed, checkpointing was
refused: the machine body alone was not joint rest. The returned current afforded no second
action, after which the combined world and machine could rest. Waiting at rest launched nothing;
remount and later wake were exact on host and card.

Reverse contact remained OPEN and independent contact formed no relation. Neither invented a
world action. The accepted card run reported ten physical launches for nine logical currents; the
tenth was one uncommitted resource retry. Host and card agreed on radiation, Standing, lineage,
world state, rest, remount, and wake.

