== Conditional consequence charts <j2-charts>

A source-neutral chart law received ordered categorical interfaces and a later consequence taxon.
At each semantic event:

```text
source interfaces meet prior chart Standing
  -> recurrence distribution returns
  -> genuinely later actual taxon arrives
  -> exact membership residual stands
  -> one reduced replacement chart returns
```

The actual consequence was not smuggled into the earlier prediction. A singleton match RIDEd;
plural support containing the actual remained `OPEN_INCLUDED`; absence of the actual remained
`OPEN_RESIDUAL`; and no case fabricated FOUND.

After twelve events the two operation regions had the same marginal recurrence distribution
$1/3:2/3$ but different conditional interiors:

```text
operation
|- drop_then_reverse   1/3 : 2/3
|  `- condition
|     |- absent             -> A
|     |- irrelevant_before  -> B
|     `- relevant_after     -> B
`- reverse_then_drop   1/3 : 2/3
   `- context
      |- code_comment  -> A
      |- conversation  -> B
      `- prose         -> B
```

Collapsing either region to its marginal quotient destroys the relation needed for later conduct.
This is an exact example of why compression must be indexed by a receiver family rather than a
scalar notion of simplicity.

== Outgoing factor and physical departure <j2-departure>

The first chart experiment replaced the active interfaces but retained a growing interior:
191 cells, 5,100 incidences and pins, 5,111 paths, and 5,195 transport terms in the final
constituent. A follow-up let the source declare the updated chart boundary as the outgoing factor
of the *joint event*. The machine committed it only after:

1. all regional contacts formed;
2. exact touched Standing-before entered joint closure;
3. the selected subcomplex passed the existing boundary-compression certificate; and
4. its exposed boundary was structurally identical to the complete joint event's exposed
   boundary.

An unmatched, OPEN, FOUND, or oriented residual arm would remain exposed and make the fourth
check refuse.

#theorem[
  Let $j:C -> E$ select a subcomplex of the complete joint event and suppose its exposed boundary
  equals the exposed boundary of $E$. Then replacing $E$ by $C$ preserves every later contact
  whose admission factors only through that exposed boundary.
]

#proof[
  Such a later contact can inspect only the shared exposed boundary. By hypothesis the boundary
  occurrence population, orientation, capabilities, and admitted transport family are identical.
  The later contact therefore receives the same input relation. The statement makes no claim
  about an observation which can access an omitted interior.
]

The implemented check is structural, not a later garbage collector or observer reconstruction.
